# CODEOWNERS — GitLab automatic reviewer routing.
# https://docs.gitlab.com/ee/user/project/codeowners/
#
# Tier behavior: this project runs on GitLab.com Free tier today.
# CODEOWNERS surfaces the assigned owner on the MR page but does NOT
# block merge on lack of code-owner approval. Required-approval
# enforcement and the sectioned [SectionName] syntax are Premium /
# Ultimate features. The file is informational at this tier; the
# audit-trail value — declared ownership, assessable by a third
# party — is real even without the enforcement gate.
#
# Self-approval note: moot on Free (no gate to satisfy). On Premium
# with "Prevent approval by author of the merge request" enabled, a
# single maintainer named here cannot satisfy the codeowner approval
# requirement on their own MR. At that point either comment out the
# global line below or add a second maintainer.
#
# Single-maintainer placeholder. Patterns are last-match-wins; the
# global owner below catches anything not covered by a more specific
# rule. Mirrors .github/CODEOWNERS so the two forge files stay in
# lockstep.

*                                       @doolin

# CI configuration — highest-impact surface. Changes here can silently
# weaken the evidence stream (severity flip, gate `when: never`,
# suppressed audit-event JSON) and still produce a green pipeline.
.gitlab-ci.yml                          @doolin
.gitlab/ci/                             @doolin
scripts/attest.mjs                      @doolin
scripts/check-coverage.mjs              @doolin
scripts/generate-oscal.js               @doolin
scripts/verify-evidence.js              @doolin
.trivyignore                            @doolin

